<title>BELGIUM: Farm ministers to agree food pesticide residue limits.</title>
<headline>Farm ministers to agree food pesticide residue limits.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers are expected on Tuesday to agree by qualified majority to update pesticide residue limits in food after a German statement calling for special treatment for baby food, EU officials said.</p>
<p>Germany, along with Sweden and Denmark, was concerned because of the prospect of having to import baby food from other EU countries where standards are lower.</p>
<p>The new rules, which cover cereals, fruit, vegetables and food products, harmonise pesticide levels in member states and introduce an EU control system.</p>
</text>
